SlimeVR Server output (airpodsvr/slimeout.py): speaks the UDP protocol of the SlimeVR tracker
  firmware so that a SlimeVR Server the user installed can do the body. Written from the protocol as
  implemented in SlimeVR-Server (MIT OR Apache-2.0); this file contains no SlimeVR code.
  SlimeVR is a trademark of SlimeVR B.V. FBT Pods is not affiliated with or endorsed by SlimeVR B.V.

Design references (ideas re-implemented, no code copied):
  SlimeVR Server — Copyright SlimeVR contributors, MIT OR Apache-2.0 —
    https://github.com/SlimeVR/SlimeVR-Server : reset types, "Stay Aligned" yaw correction
    (rest detection, relaxed-pose targets), LegTweaks floor clip and skating correction.
HMD-Poser — Copyright (c) 2024 Pico-AI-Team, MIT licence — https://github.com/Pico-AI-Team/HMD-Poser :
  airpodsvr/hmdposer.py is a NumPy re-implementation of its network and input features so its
  published checkpoint can be run without PyTorch. The checkpoint is NOT shipped: the user downloads
  it from the HMD-Poser repository (Advanced -> pose model). It was trained on AMASS, so it is for
  non-commercial research use only and must not be redistributed.
Training data (if you train the pose model): AMASS and SMPL+H, non-commercial research
  licences; model weights trained on them must not be redistributed or used commercially.

